      "seconds": 112.124,
      "answer": "**Three-Part Study Guide: Pump Operation Procedure**\n=====================================================\n\n**Part 1: Inspection**\n--------------------\n\nBefore starting the pump, inspect the inlet for debris and check that the pressure gauge reads zero.\n\n*   **Practice Question:** What is the first step to take before starting the pump?\n\n    Answer: Inspect the inlet for debris and check that the pressure gauge reads zero.\n\n**Part 2: Operation**\n------------------\n\n1.  Open the inlet valve before starting the pump.\n2.  Stop the pump if pressure exceeds 90 kPa.\n\n*   **Practice Question:** What should you do if the pressure exceeds 90 kPa?\n\n    Answer: Stop the pump.\n\n**Part 3: Shutdown**\n------------------\n\n1.  Turn the motor off.\n2.  Close the inlet valve.\n3.  Record the final pressure.\n4.  Do not open the casing while the pump is pressurized.\n\n*   **Practice Question:** What should you do after turning the motor off?\n\n    Answer: Close the inlet valve and record the final pressure.\n\n**Short Answer Key**\n-------------------\n\n1.  What is the purpose of inspecting the inlet before starting the pump?\n    Answer: To check for debris and ensure the pressure gauge reads zero.\n2.  What is the condition to stop the pump?\n    Answer: When the pressure exceeds 90 kPa.\n3.  What should you do after turning the motor off?\n    Answer: Close the inlet valve and record the final pressure.\n\n> Coverage check: 3 of 3 source sections have no linked substantive passage in this answer. The response may be incomplete; full coverage is not verified.",
